# question: As the data steward responsible for maintaining the integrity and compliance of our hospital research data warehouse, I need to generate a precise count of distinct patients who meet both of the following criteria: 1) they have at least one documented resuscitation directive coded under the SNOMED CT concept for ‘For resuscitation’ (304252001) or any of its descendant sub‑codes, and 2) they have at least one microbiology biomolecule presence result that is explicitly coded as ‘Negative’ (260385009) or any of its descendant sub‑codes. This metric is essential for evaluating the intersection of advance care planning and microbiological testing outcomes across our patient population, and will inform both quality improvement initiatives and regulatory reporting. Please provide the single numeric result that satisfies these conditions.
# expected_compliant: true
# expected_rules: none
# origin: test set T3 (worded by the other model)
# notes: PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#> PREFIX snomed: <http://snomed.info/id/> PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?g) AS ?patients) WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?a a sphn:ResuscitationDirective ; sphn:hasCode ?a_c . ?a_c rdf:type snomed:304252001 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") . ?b a sphn:MicrobiologyBiomoleculePresenceResult ; sphn:hasCode ?b_c . ?b_c rdf:type snomed:260385009 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") . } }
PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#>
PREFIX snomed: <http://snomed.info/id/>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?g) AS ?patients) WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?a a sphn:ResuscitationDirective ; sphn:hasCode ?a_c . ?a_c rdf:type snomed:304252001 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") . ?b a sphn:MicrobiologyBiomoleculePresenceResult ; sphn:hasCode ?b_c . ?b_c rdf:type snomed:260385009 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") . } }
